ugs or add new features  is also managed by google as well  so next what do we mean by application  platform  in this sense an application platform  provides  something that can actually host the  applications of your choice  be they container based applications  or they can also be traditional  applications  our application platform is based on  completely open source projects  for example kubernetes sdo  k-native techton to name a few  now the platform is also designed for  enterprises in mind  that have large complex needs  it could be security requirements  operational requirements  governance requirements there's many  many requirements that our enterprises  need to cater for and anthos provides  all those enterprises with the  capability to manage  all those needs be they large or small  next our customers also want the ability  to  have access to faster modernization  and with anthos we provide tooling to  help our customers  to have no touch migrations from  traditional workloads into modern  workloads  and not just the actual applications  themselves but also  the platform and we provide tools  to help our customers modernize the way  they even manage the platform itself  next anthos provides greater consistency  now it's very common that across our  enterprise customers  that they may deploy anthos in not just  a single  deployment option like in gcp but may  want to deploy this across  hybrid environments as well as  multi-cloud environments  so in that sense the importance to have  a single pane of glass and a single  definition  of how they want security policies  or even just general configurations need  to be kept in sync across  all those environments and andos  provides  methods to achieve that  finally anthos is a multi-cloud and  hybrid cloud  platform it's completely software-based  which means  it runs inside on-premises data centers  inside gcp and also in other clouds  now anthos didn't happen overnight  it is actually a combination of decades